## Why This Is Asked

Tests for data-import flows are common in cloud applications. This question evaluates practical E2E thinking at a beginner level, covering end-to-end flow, UI feedback, and data integrity.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end flow of uploading data and handling background processing
- Mocking backend services (job queue) for deterministic, reliable tests
- Data seeding to ensure predictable idempotent behavior
- Verifying UI progress indicators and downloadable summary reports

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Playwright snippet illustrating route mocking and upload
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test('data import workflow with progress and idempotency', async ({ page }) => {
  // Seed database with existing records for idempotency testing
  await seedTestData();

  // Mock the job queue response
  await page.route('**/api/import', async (route) => {
    await route.fulfill({
      status: 200,
      body: JSON.stringify({ jobId: 'test-job-123', status: 'processing' })
    });
  });

  // Upload CSV fixture
  await page.setInputFiles('input[type="file"]', 'fixtures/test-data-500-rows.csv');

  // Verify live progress updates
  await expect(page.locator('.progress-bar')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('.progress-text')).toContainText('100%');

  // Verify invalid rows are highlighted
  await expect(page.locator('.invalid-row')).toHaveCount(5);

  // Download and verify summary report
  const [download] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForEvent('download'),
    page.click('.download-summary')
  ]);

  const report = await download.text();
  expect(report).toContain('Total: 500');
  expect(report).toContain('Valid: 495');
  expect(report).toContain('Invalid: 5');

  // Test idempotency - re-upload same file
  await page.setInputFiles('input[type="file"]', 'fixtures/test-data-500-rows.csv');
  await page.waitForSelector('.upload-complete');

  // Verify no duplicates were created
  const recordCount = await getRecordCount();
  expect(recordCount).toBe(500);
});
```

## Why This Question Matters

This question assesses your understanding of end-to-end data isolation, cross-region replication, retention governance, and PII redaction across a data lake, transformed layers, and BI dashboards—essential skills for building enterprise-compliant multi-tenant systems.

## Key Concepts to Demonstrate

- Multi-tenant data isolation across raw and transformed layers
- Per-tenant retention and purge workflows with full auditability
- Cross-region replication latency and consistency guarantees
- PII redaction verification across caches and dashboards
- Seed data design and deterministic testing signals

## Code Example

```javascript
// Seed tenants for deterministic E2E tests
const tenants = [
  { id: 't1', name: 'Acme Corp', region: 'us-east-1' },
  { id: 't2', name: 'Globex', region: 'eu-west-1' }
];

// Simulate event streams from mobile and web
async function seedEventStream(tenant, source) {
  const events = generateEvents(tenant.id, source, 1000);
  await publishToIngestTopic(tenant.region, events);
}

// Verify isolation: ensure t1 cannot access t2 data
async function verifyIsolation() {
  const t1Raw = await queryRawLake('t1');
  const t2Raw = await queryRawLake('t2');
  expect(t1Raw).not.toContainTenantData('t2');
  expect(t2Raw).not.toContainTenantData('t1');
}

// Verify PII redaction in transformed views
async function verifyRedaction() {
  const transformed = await queryTransformedView('t1');
  expect(transformed).toHaveRedacted('email');
  expect(transformed).toHaveRedacted('phone');
}
```

## Verification Matrix

| Layer | Isolation | Redaction | Retention |
|-------|-----------|-----------|------------|
| Raw Lake | ✓ | N/A | ✓ |
| Transformed | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |
| Cache | ✓ | ✓ | N/A |
| BI Dashboard | ✓ | ✓ | N/A |

## Essential Metrics

- **Isolation violations**: Zero cross-tenant data leaks
- **Redaction coverage**: 100% of defined PII fields
- **Replication lag**: < 5s for sync, < 60s for async regions
- **Retention accuracy**: Auto-purge at tenant-specified TTL
- **Query latency**: P95 < 500ms for dashboard queries

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of end-to-end testing in a complex, multi-region, event-sourced delivery application. It checks whether the candidate can design tests that cover data isolation, cross-region convergence, failure handling, and compliance scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- Event-sourced E2E flows with Kafka domain topics and region-specific read models
- Cross-region consistency and latency budget validation
- Multi-tenant data isolation and DSAR (Data Subject Access Request) compliance
- Fault injection including regional outages and retry mechanisms
- Observability integration and deterministic seed data

## Code Example
```javascript
// Seed deterministic test data and publish events to Kafka; verify read-model convergence
const seedOrder = { id: 'ORD-123', tenantId: 'tenant-acme', region: 'us-east' };

await kafka.publish('orders.us-east', { 
  eventType: 'OrderPlaced', 
  payload: seedOrder, 
  timestamp: '2026-01-15T10:00:00Z' 
});

await kafka.publish('drivers.us-east', {
  eventType: 'DriverAssigned',
  payload: { orderId: 'ORD-123', driverId: 'DRV-456' }
});

// Verify real-time WebSocket delivery to clients
const wsUpdate = await waitForWebSocketMessage('rider-client', 'ETAUpdated');
expect(wsUpdate.payload.eta).toBeWithinSLA();

// Validate cross-region read-model convergence
const readModel = await readModelClient.query('us-west', 'orders', { id: 'ORD-123' });
expect(readModel.status).toEqual('confirmed');
expect(readModel.convergenceTime).toBeLessThan(SLA_THRESHOLD_MS);

// Verify tenant isolation
const crossTenantResult = await readModelClient.query('us-east', 'orders', { 
  id: 'ORD-123', 
  tenantId: 'tenant-foreign' 
});
expect(crossTenantResult.accessDenied).toBe(true);

// DSAR deletion verification
await dsarService.requestDeletion('customer-789');
await waitForEventProcessing();
const piiCheck = await readModelClient.scanAllRegions('customer-789');
expect(piiCheck.found).toBe(false);

// Region failover test
await regionOutageSimulator.failover('us-east', 'us-west');
const failoverState = await readModelClient.getState('us-west', 'ORD-123');
expect(failoverState.reconstructed).toBe(true);
```
